  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Spikes in policy uncertainty about export controls, investment screening, or subsidy rules tied to the tech rivalry reduce expected returns and increase tail-risk perceptions, causing investors to lower aggregate risk appetite and reallocate into safer assets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">us_political_shift</data>
</edge>
