<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::portfolio_reallocation" target="global_ai_power_shift::investor_sentiment" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">An increased net portfolio_reallocation rate away from Chinese tech and toward U.S./allied AI firms improves funding conditions and observable flows into those beneficiaries, directly boosting investor_sentiment for the receiving markets and firms.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">global_ai_power_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::portfolio_reallocation" target="iran_gulf_conflict::capital_flow_to_equities" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Rapid portfolio reallocation away from China/Asia tech into safe assets during tech-rivalry shocks drives global risk-off flows that include withdrawals from Gulf and emerging-market equities, reducing net capital flows to equities there.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::portfolio_reallocation" target="russia_ukraine_war::bond_yield" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">Large reallocations triggered by intensified US–China tech rivalry (risk-off moves out of Asian/Tec h equities into safe assets) widen risk premia on emerging-market and frontier credit, lifting sovereign and corporate bond yields relevant to Russia/Ukraine financing.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::portfolio_reallocation" target="us_political_shift::investor_risk_appetite" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained large-scale capital flows out of contested-tech sectors or into safe-haven assets reduce liquidity and push down forward returns in higher-risk segments, which mechanically lowers investors' willingness to maintain elevated risk exposures.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">us_political_shift</data>
</edge>
